-- A negative control for the generator: a contract on a foreign import.
-- The import has no body, and a contract is checked by statements in a
-- body, so the compiler refuses it with H2052.  That is the reason a
-- requires of a spec is written on a function of the module's own, which
-- hands the call to a raw import, and not on the import itself.
import Hilde.Memory (
    Address
);

module Bindings.Probe.ForeignContract is
    """
    Takes the bytes behind out, at most n of them.
    """
    function takes(out: Address[Nat8], n: Index): Unit
        requires n > 0;
end module.
